# SEO and launch leftovers

Do **not** start this work during routine homepage visual edits.

**Bring this up** when any of these are true:

- The designer says the site is almost done, launching, or ready for SEO
- Inner pages are being built (About, Services, Projects, Careers, Contact)
- A form, quote flow, or careers application is added
- Domain, hosting, or indexing is being set up

Until the rest of the site is ready: keep unfinished menu items as coming soon; do not invent layouts or business facts. Home, About, Services hub, Straight-Shaft, Contact, and Careers are live; do not run a full SEO/GEO pass unless asked.

